# An action described by the verb "to [[march]]".
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1862|author=Various|title=Atlantic Monthly, Vol. 10, No. 61, November, 1862|chapter=|edition=|url=http://www.gutenberg.org/etext/11158
|passage=A pianoforte is desirable, to lead the singing, and accompany the plays, gymnastics, frequent '''marchings''', and dancing, when that is taught,&mdash;which it should be.}}
#* {{RQ:Carlyle French Revolution|text=But of the '''marchings''' and retreatings of these Six-thousand no Xenophon exists. Nothing, but an inarticulate hum, of cursing and sooty frenzy, surviving dubious in the memory of ages!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1917|author=War Department|title=Manual for Noncommissioned Officers and Privates of Infantry|chapter=|edition=|url=http://www.gutenberg.org/etext/10908
|passage=All steps and '''marchings''' executed from a halt, except right step, begin with the left foot.}}

